{"_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "The New Waiter", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Colombian Customs", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 6, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 5, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.3", "type": "level"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"content": " Explain customs and appropriate behaviour at work and in different countries, using a wider range of expressions and formulas. ", "type": "primary"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_8"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"content": "engenn8le05ob06re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"contents": [{"content": " The Position of Not", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " In English, the adverb  <span class=\"italic\">not</span> usually goes after the auxiliary verb or \u201cbe\u201d to form the negative. <br/><br/> You can use the adverb not in other positions in some cases.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Usually, we find the adverb not in conjunction with an auxiliary verb or \u201cbe\u201d in a negative sentence.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Example:<br/>  <span class=\"italic\">If you do <span class=\"strong\">not</span> mind me asking, where are you from?</span><br/>  <span class=\"italic\">You will <span class=\"strong\">not</span> regret it, trust me.</span><br/>  <span class=\"italic\">You shouldn't leave any food uneaten = You should <span class=\"strong\">not</span>leave any food uneaten. </span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When you use the long form instead of the contraction, you emphasize the negation of the verb.", "type": "text"}, {"content": " You also find <span class=\"italic\">not</span> <span class=\"strong\">before</span> a verb in the Infinitive.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Example:<br/> <span class=\"italic\">I'll try <span class=\"strong\">not</span> to upset them too much!", "type": "text"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": " Should and Be Supposed To ", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the modal  <span class=\"strong\">should</span> or the  structure  <span class=\"strong\">be supposed to</span> when you want to talk about expectations, obligations or arrangements.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You can use  <span class=\"strong\">be supposed to</span> to talk about situations in the present or future that are expected to happen. <br/><br/> The structure is:<br/><br/>  Subject + To be + supposed to + verb<br/><br/>  <span class=\"italic\">Sharing information with their new colleagues is something they're <span class=\"strong\">supposed to do</span> .</span> <br/><br/>  **Pronunciation tip**:<br/> When you say be supposed to, you link the /d/ and /t/ sounds together.  <br/><br/> Like this:<br/> Be suppose_to", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I'm supposed to spend a year there for an exchange program.  ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I heard that you shouldn't leave any food uneaten if you're invited at someone's house.", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "uncomfortable", "type": "name"}, {"content": "eeling unease about something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: People feel uncomfortable when you leave food on your plate.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le05ob06aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": " These are words you use when you talk about different cultures.", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "uneaten", "type": "name"}, {"content": "food that is left on a plate", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You shouldn't leave any food uneaten if you're invited to someone's house.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le05ob06aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "elder", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a person of a greater age", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Our elders feel uncomfortable when they see food uneaten on a plate.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le05ob06aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "accommodating", "type": "name"}, {"content": " to do something nice for someone, a favor", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We always try to be accommodating to our guests.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le05ob06aud04", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "lost in translation", "type": "name"}, {"content": " an attempt to translate something and the original meaning can not be perfectly translated into the other language.", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: My Japanese house guest didn't understand that expression. Some things are just lost in translation.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le05ob06aud05", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "display", "type": "name"}, {"content": " a show of feelings for everyone to see", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We like to focus our public displays of emotions on something positive, like dancing.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le05ob06aud06", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to defuse", "type": "name"}, {"content": " to make a dangerous situation safer", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The two men's argument was beginning to get serious, but Julie defused the situation with a joke.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le05ob06aud07", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Brainstorm some popular local dishes from your country. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Say which one is your favorite and explain why to a partner.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "What food would you recomme